A||N||8||rockcrawl||'88 Suspension by Lotus||||5||
Z||000000||rockcrawl||09-04-2000||04:07 PM||||I recently read that the 88 Fiero suspension being designed by Lotus is just a fairytale. I remember a few years ago at a car show there was an emblem dealer with tons of old emblems. I remember looking at the fiero emblems and seeing one that said "Suspension by Lotus" displayed with the Fiero stuff. Obviously this guy thought it was from a Fiero. I was just wondering if anyone knows how the rumor got started? It seems like everyone thinks the '88 had a Lotus designed suspension.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Black88GT||09-04-2000||04:32 PM||||yeah I hate that, when '88 owners put those damned badges from POS Isuzu's that says "Suspension by Lotus". I remember on ebay some guy paid 90 bucks for 2 of them!! I think it got started because some guy on the team worked for Lotus or something like that.  Maybe someone else has a better answer.  <P><BR>||||reg||8
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||09-04-2000||04:41 PM||||I think one of the car magazines doing tests on an 88 said the rear suspension was Lotus based. It probably sprung from that. <P>Meanwhile, Delorean basically ripped off the design of the whole car.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||09-04-2000||05:36 PM||||The '88 suspension was <B>loosely</B> based on an old <B>prototype</B> Lotus suspension.  The suspension was not built or designed by Lotus although it does make for some good marketing. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||09-04-2000||06:34 PM||||In actuallity, the suspension on an 88 Fiero is the same configuration that Lotus designed for the Esprit (sp?) Using unequal length control arms to aid in the lower angles of the car and still make it handle and ride well. If you read the 1988 Fiero changes Brochure put out by Pontiac that lists all the changes to an 88 Fiero, The exact wording (which somehow the press messed up) is: "..the suspension was redesigned simular to exotic cars such as Lotus, to provide better control and ride." <BR>The brochure was a single page that showed a monochrome Med Metallic Red GT on top and listed the changes. It even lists that mid-year they will come with variable power steering. Although the PS never made it to a production car.||||reg||1
Z||000005||PJ||09-04-2000||11:03 PM||||BTW, the proper name for the rear struts on an '88 is NOT McPherson. The correct term for them are Chapman Struts. Invented by Colin Chapman, founder of Lotus.<P>Damn, I want an Elise. The racing version.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||gixxer||09-05-2000||12:07 AM||||Oh yeah? take this PJ!<BR>"Not generally known, the geometry of the strut type IFS used on almost all small cars today - credited to GM (and later Ford) engineer Earle S. MacPherson - first appeared on another French car, the Cottin et Desgouttes, in 1926." <BR>Ripped shamelessly from the book Race Car Chassis (Design and Contruction).<BR>Oh yeah, if the strut is used up front, it's called a MacPherson Strut. If it's used in back, it's called a Chapman Strut.<BR>Just thought everybody should know! Heh..||||reg||1
Z||000007||Wannabe||09-05-2000||08:47 AM||||Unless your car only steers by the rear wheels  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||MikeSchaefer||09-05-2000||02:41 PM||||Every ricer in America will also swear up and down his car has a lotus suspension, or is powered by acura.  I'm embarrassed to say that I used to believe the Fiero Lotus Fairy Tail myself though.  I kind of like the idea of not knowing certain things about people's cars, like if they have a K&N filter, or if they use Splitfire sparkplugs, etc.  I love to see a junky little ricer pull up with his "lotus suspension" and 200 other little stickers or badges from other cars, it makes me feel really good about driving my Fiero, with a genuine suspension by Pontiac.<BR>Michael Schaefer||||reg||2
